    {
      "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
      "body": "Ran this branch on an MI355X (gfx950) with `rocm/sgl-dev:v0.5.21-rocm10-mi35x-20261007`, whose aiter is `e7d2453f2` (2026-09-25):\n\n```\nIMPORT OK\n[CI Test Method] TestCompactAttentionHip.test_matches_torch_over_both_caches_splits_and_empty_rows\nRan 1 test in 5.361s\nOK\n```\n\nTwo things that confirms:\n\n- The import resolves. On main it raises `ModuleNotFoundError` for `_gluon_kernels.gfx950.attention.pa_decode_sparse`, which aiter removed in ROCm/aiter#4919 on 2026-09-18 — see #43765.\n- The numerics hold, including the change of `m` into the scaled base-2 domain. The test compares against a torch softmax-with-sink reference at `rtol=2e-2` over both packed layouts, `splits` 1 and 4, the second cache, `-1` slots and a sink-only row, so the dropped `m * (SCALE * RCP_LN2)` at the sink and `Max` store is covered rather than assumed.\n\nWorth noting CI has not exercised this: every AMD job on this PR is skipped because `pr-gate` is failing for the missing `run-ci` label, so the above is currently the only run of the test.\n",
